<title>INDIA: Indian soybean firm, oil steady, meal up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean firm, oil steady, meal up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained firm on poor arrivals in central Indian markets, with prices up by 250-300 rupees per tonne on good demand from processing plants, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand from vanaspati manufacturers but soyoil refined was steady. Business volume was dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices remained bullish on good export demand against limited supplies. Soymeal yellow was up by $3-4 per tonne in export and was up 100 rupees per tonne in local market.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $267-270 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) westcoast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $97-100 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,400-3,450 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
